            <ArticleTitle>Clinical assessment and pharmacologic treatment of pain in children: cancer as a model for the management of chronic or persistent pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>64-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper describes methods of assessment and pharmacologic management for chronic or persistent pain in children. This report will be a clinical one, derived from the experiences of a pediatric oncologist (P.M.Z.) and a pediatric pain consultant (L.K.Z.). Case reports will illustrate clinical assessment and management strategies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
